# Import test fixtures are BYTES, not text.
#
# `webapp/tests/unit/read.test.ts` asserts that a CRLF file parses as CRLF, that
# a BOM is detected and stripped, and that windows-1252 bytes decode through the
# C1 table rather than as ISO-8859-1. Every one of those assertions is about the
# exact bytes on disk — and git's autocrlf/eol normalisation rewrites precisely
# those bytes on checkout. A normalised `crlf-bom.csv` still passes its test on
# the machine that created it and disarms it for everybody else: the test keeps
# reporting green while the dialect it exists to cover is no longer in the file.
#
# `-text` turns every kind of line-ending conversion off for these paths.
webapp/tests/fixtures/import/*.csv -text
webapp/tests/fixtures/import/*.xlsx -text binary
webapp/tests/fixtures/import/*.xls  -text binary
webapp/tests/fixtures/import/*.numbers -text binary
